-- title:
--   Galois representation attached to a mod-p Hecke eigensystem
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $p \nmid N$, let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers, and let $k$ be an integer weight which is also given as a natural number $k_n$ with $(k_n : \mathbb{Z}) = k$. Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and let $\theta : \mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ N\ k\ S \to F$ be a ring homomorphism, where `heckeAlgebra N k S` is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of cusp forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. The assertion is that there is a group homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) = (\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ with the following three properties. First, $\rho$ factors through a finite level: there is an intermediate field $L$ with $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq L \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Second, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the matrix underlying $\rho(\sigma)$ has trace $\theta(T_\ell)$, the image under $\theta$ of the element `heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓS`. Third, for $\ell$, $A$ and $\sigma$ as in the second clause, that matrix has determinant $(\ell : F)^{k_n - 1}$, the exponent being the truncated natural-number difference.
--
--   This is the existence of the two-dimensional mod-$p$ Galois representation attached to a Hecke eigensystem of weight $k$ and level $N$ prime to $p$, with the Frobenius traces prescribed by the eigenvalues of $T_\ell$ and the determinant given by the $(k-1)$st power of the cyclotomic character, in the form due to Deligne. It is used in the project to compare twists of such eigensystems, via [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.natCast_pow_twist_eq_natCast_pow_weight_sub_one_of_twist_mem`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.natCast_pow_twist_eq_natCast_pow_weight_sub_one_of_twist_mem).
